    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance visible from both directions on the road.\n• Mark the single driveway entrance clearly so responders can identify it quickly at night or in reduced visibility.\n• Clear vegetation along both sides of the access drive to maintain an unobstructed travel path for emergency vehicles.\n• Trim tree branches overhanging the access drive to allow full-size emergency vehicles to pass without obstruction.\n• Designate and mark a turnaround area near the main residence large enough for a fire apparatus or ambulance to reverse direction.\n• Keep the turnaround area free of parked vehicles, equipment, and stored materials at all times.\n• Install a sign or marker at the detached structure to help responders distinguish it from the main residence on arrival.\n• Keep the parking area clear of vehicles that could block responder staging space near the residence.\n• If perimeter fencing includes a gate across the access drive, keep that gate unlocked or install a Knox Box or responder-compatible lock to allow immediate entry.\n• Post the property address on or near any driveway gate so responders can confirm the correct property before entry.\n• Thin dense vegetation alongside the access drive so responders on foot can move between the drive and the open terrain without obstruction."
  },
