    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly next to the structure to create open space between the plants and the building.\n• Thin the tree cluster to increase spacing between individual trees and reduce how easily fire can move from one tree to the next.\n• Remove or cut back shrubs and brush growing along the driveway to keep it clear for vehicles to pass through safely.\n• Trim any overhanging tree branches that extend over the driveway or roofline.\n• Cut grass near the structure short and keep it mowed regularly, especially during dry periods.\n• Clear dead grass, leaves, and loose plant material that has collected against or near the structure.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure so there is open ground between their canopies and the building.\n• Remove brush from areas where it connects directly to trees or shrubs near the structure, breaking up the continuous path of vegetation.\n• Keep the area immediately surrounding the structure free of shrub regrowth by checking and cutting it back regularly.\n• Clear brush and tall grass from the edges of all driveways and access routes to maintain open lanes for emergency vehicles.\n• Thin shrubs in the brush area nearest the structure so individual plants are separated by open ground rather than growing together in a dense mass."
  },
